# sqlite = require("bun:sqlite"); loaded = require(name); loaded()   built with two entry points, main.cjs and other.cjs
# A load under a name that is put together at run time evaluates nothing, and of the program's files it answers the entry points. A module of the library that is written in JavaScript is in the image only if seen code names it:
# the one that the program requires has run and stays in the answer, and the one that nobody names stays unreached. A native module has no code to run. Its object is in the answer as an object that the analysis follows,
# and being there is no use of it, so nothing comes into the image for it
